    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0573" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg531"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 27, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: With reference to the unofficial
                    letters which passed between us on the 6th instant, I send you a copy of an
                    order on the subject of intercourse with blockaded ports, which has been
                    addressed by Vice-Admiral Sir Alex. Milne to the officers in command of her
                    Majesty’s ships under his orders.</p>
                <p>Yours, faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d426-a1.xml" xpointer="d426-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
